      "text_raw": "The non-idealities of the DA\nconversion give rise to sev-\neral specifications, such as\nthe DNL and the INL.\nThe DNL is the largest\nstep ever minus one LSB. It\nis the largest deviation from\na regular step.\nThe INL is the largest\ndeviation from the average\nslope.\nIf this slope is not right,\nthen a gain error is found.\nThis slope must go through\nzero. If not, an offset occurs.",
      "text": "The non-idealities of the DA conversion give rise to several specifications, such as the DNL and the INL. The DNL is the largest step ever minus one LSB. It is the largest deviation from a regular step. The INL is the largest deviation from the average slope. If this slope is not right, then a gain error is found. This slope must go through zero. If not, an offset occurs."
    }
